{"lyrics":"[Intro]\n[00:01.26] We'll be here, lettin' go\n[00:11.94] Chopsquad\n[00:13.44] Someone needs to let me know\n[00:16.36] I'm havin' problems lettin' go\n[00:23.82] Overload (Haha)\n[Chorus]\n[00:25.74] I'm havin' problems lettin' go\n[00:31.48] I need solutions, someone let me know\n[00:38.36] I can't help it when I lose control\n[00:44.60] This a emotional overdose\n[Verse 1]\n[00:51.78] I tried to talk but you ain't givin' feedback\n[00:54.74] My depression really hungry and you feed that\n[00:57.78] You say you love me, but I don't know if you mean that\n[01:01.04] And I'm scared (Haha)\n[01:04.90] You've been helpin' me avoid a relapse\n[01:07.76] All your love and affection, I need that\n[01:10.76] You prolly tired of me, yeah, I understand (Haha)\n[01:17.58] I'ma make the song bleed, need a Kleenex\n[01:20.66] Girl, you make me happy like a kid at recess\n[01:23.68] But when you mad, you make me feel like a reject, no jerk\n[01:30.62] You separate my angels from my demons\n[01:33.20] Pinch myself 'cause it feels like I'm dreamin\n[01:36.24] But when you not here for me, the nightmares begin\n[Chorus]\n[01:43.60] I'm havin' problems lettin' go\n[01:49.30] I need solutions, someone let me know (Haha)\n[01:56.20] I can't help it when I lose control\n[02:02.44] This a emotional overdose (Huh)\n[Verse 2]\n[02:09.86] I cannot pretend that I don't care\n[02:12.10] Hittin' below the belt, that shit hurt, and it's not fair\n[02:15.38] Traumatized thoughts, girl, that shit gon' leave a mark, yeah\n[02:19.28] Imagine takin' a bullet to the heart, yeah\n[02:22.70] Nowadays, I don't know where home is\n[02:25.74] But you're the closest thing to a home I have\n[02:28.96] But right about now I feel homeless\n[02:32.44] Back to the heartbreak flashbacks\n[Chorus]\n[02:35.62] I'm havin' problems lettin' go\n[02:41.22] I need solutions, someone let me know\n[02:48.10] I can't help it when I lose control\n[02:54.34] This a emotional overdose\n[Verse 3]\n[03:01.68] Woke up on the wrong side of the bed\n[03:08.18] Baby, rest your weary head\n[03:13.86] We been goin' through this sadness and dread\n[03:21.08] Put your hand, in my dreads\n[03:26.32] So, you can feel what I been thinkin'\n[03:34.32] I know that the past leaves scars\n[03:39.74] Light-headed, but, I still got a heavy heart\n[03:46.10] I know what drugs I take, the shit too far\n[03:52.50] But if I don't take them, I'll be falling apart\n[03:59.98] We don't want that now, do we?, uh\n[04:05.72] Walk on the beach in a date to the movies, mm\n[04:12.98] We don't want that now, do we?\n[04:18.64] Walk on the beach in a date to the movies\n[04:26.02] Here we go again\n[04:32.26] I thought that this may be the end\n[04:39.02] All I know is: I'ma sin\n[04:43.42] With or without you, oh\n[04:51.50] Yeah, talking to the percs again\n[04:56.12] I hear the voices again\n[04:58.68] All I know is hurt again\n[05:02.52] Is it worth it then?\n[05:04.96] Are these percs working then?, I can't tell\n[05:11.42] I'ma hide the pills in the Chanel\n[05:17.86] Full room, but, I'm all alone\n[05:24.36] She not on my cellular phone\n[05:27.04] I thought that this was a happy home\n[05:36.96] In the underworld is where I roam\n[05:43.76] All I know is, I need peace\n[05:50.12] I need you, but you don't need me\n[05:53.72] Yeah, don't you see the irony?\n[06:02.96] All girls are just the same to me\n[06:09.88] I don't think I'll ever catch a break\n[06:13.12] I'ma take these pills to the face\n[06:16.40] I don't know if I wanna be awake the next da-a-a-ay-ay\n[06:22.90] All I know, is that I need a break\n[06:26.02] I'ma take these percs to the face\n[06:27.92] I don't know if I wanna be awake the next da-ay\n[06:36.12] Listening to Kurt Cobain\n[06:42.16] Trying to figure out, what you sayin', to me\n[06:48.50] I guess, it's a Nirvana thing\n[06:55.56] Gave her a bullet for her valentine\n[06:58.86] All I wanted was her, be mine\n[07:01.66] I ain't really want her to be blind\n[07:05.36] All I wanted was her to be mine\n[07:07.70] I ain't really want her to be blind\n[07:12.70] You put up for sides\n[07:17.98] You don't need me, bitch, you need God\n[07:24.02] Ayy, the devil keep on playing his eyes\n[07:30.66] He gon' need a doctor, a nigga knows\n[07:33.90] I thought you came to make me whole\n[07:40.18] But you really came to take my soul\n[07:46.86] I let you have it, take control\n[07:52.34] But if you hold on, please, no letting go\n[08:00.02] They said, \"We should take it slow\"\n[08:06.12] But, I think we should take it home\n[08:11.96] I'm really bad at letting go\n[08:16.34] I get attached, and you should know\n[08:25.88] I love the way you make it snow\n[08:29.26] You take my heart, then make it cold\n[08:38.68] It feels like, you're out of my reach\n[08:45.10] It feels like, you're out of my league\n[08:51.56] These demons comin' out of me\n[08:58.04] It's really, something fun to see\n[09:04.10] Making love, ain't no more make believe\n[09:10.70] If you don't want my love, then leave\n[09:18.06] I was caught up in the past\n[09:24.60] I know that it never lasts\n[09:29.02] But, every time I make you mad\n[09:37.60] I think that'll be the last, uh\n[09:43.40] Now it's my time, where the percs at?\n[09:46.64] Where the drugs at?, Shit, I need that\n[09:49.94] Ever since you ain't been giving me no feedback\n[09:53.24] I been feeling like I need some more feedback\n[09:56.38] Now, It's my time, where the percs at?\n[09:59.62] Where the drugs at?, 'Cause, I need that\n[10:02.92] Ever since you ain't been giving me no feedback\n[10:06.14] I need morphine, bad\n[10:11.34] Would you give your all to me?\n[10:17.88] Would you even stall for me?\n[10:23.58] Would you hospital call for me?\n[10:34.48] Yeah, fire girl, OD\n[Chorus]\n[10:44.18] I'm havin' problems lettin' go\n[10:57.24] I need solutions, someone let me know\n[11:03.96] I can't help it when I lose control\n[11:09.78] This a emotional overdose","words":[[0.76,0.98,"[Intro]"],[1.0,1.02,"